{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Thus says</b> — Elihu said: \"Behold, all these El does; [He does] times three with a man.\" The meaning is that He warns him, and if he does not heed, He punishes on the fourth occasion. Yefet said: on the fourth generation, if all the generations were wicked. The Gaon [Saadia] said: three offences I forgave him, and this fourth one I will not forgive. Now in the case of Damascus, Gaza, Tyre, Edom, and the Ammonites — it is always the fourth [occasion] that they did evil to Jacob; and in the case of Moab, that they did evil to Esau, and both are sons of Isaac — therefore he mentioned \"times\" in his prophecy. And we have not found the like in the books of all the extant prophets." "<b>Because they threshed</b> — This refers to Hazael, who did evil to Israel and made them like dust for threshing. The meaning of \"they threshed Gilead with iron sledges\" (the ketiv reading דושם) — either Israel fled from it, and he was plowing through Gilead. And it is written: \"Hazael smote… all the land of Gilead.\""], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The opening quotation is from Job 33:29, Elihu's speech, which Ibn Ezra invokes to explain the idiom 'for three transgressions and for four'.", 1 "Ibn Ezra reads the ketiv דושם as 'they threshed them,' referring to Hazael's acts; the minimal note on Gilead follows the supercommentary tradition identifying the referent."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:47.876848819Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}